<title>PORTUGAL: PRESS DIGEST - PORTUGAL -- AUG 12.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - PORTUGAL -- AUG 12.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are some stories in Portuguese newspapers.</p>
<p>PUBLICO</p>
<p>*Tension high, government prepares sanctions against TAP-Air Portugal pilots who refuse to fly alleging sickness. Company reported first half operating profit of 2.3 billion escudos against 1.3 billion loss same period last year.</p>
<p>DIARIO ECONOMICO</p>
<p>*Portuguese Hotel Associations says could lose six billion escudos in revenues if disruption at TAP continues through to the end of September.</p>
<p>($1=185 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3538254</p>
</text>
